course: dictionary
lesson: 7097
title: Peacemaker and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A peacemaker is a person who helps people stop fighting and become friends again. Look at the two parts: peace and maker. A maker is someone who makes something, so a peacemaker makes peace. The context helps too: «It begins with the Beatitudes, blessings for people the world often overlooks: the poor in spirit, those who mourn, the meek, the merciful, the pure in heart and the peacemakers.» Peacemakers are in a list of good people, so they are seen as special.
explain: Think of a playground quarrel. Two pupils are shouting, then a friend steps between them and says, "Let's listen to each other." That friend is playing the peacemaker. Some people are natural peacemakers, who calm things down without being asked.
explain: The word also appears in the Bible. Jesus said, «Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called children of God». Christians believe that peacemakers do God's work, so the word has a church meaning as well as an everyday one.
fact: A peacemaker is a person who helps people or groups stop fighting and make friends again.
fact: Peace plus maker: a peacemaker makes peace.
fact: In the Bible, Jesus said «Blessed are the peacemakers», and Christians believe peacemakers do God's work.
fact: Informally, a peacemaker is someone in a family or class who often calms arguments down.
fact: Useful phrases are «play the peacemaker», «act as peacemaker» and «a natural peacemaker».
exercise: What is a peacemaker? | A teacher who gives out homework | A loud person who shouts the most in class | Someone who starts fights to win | *A person who helps people stop fighting and make friends again
exercise: «Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called children of God.» Find and copy the word that names the people Jesus blesses. | God | peace | children | *peacemakers
exercise: Which phrase means someone who calms arguments down without being asked? | *A natural peacemaker | A fierce fighter | A loud argument | A lost cause
test: In the list «the poor in spirit, those who mourn, the meek, the merciful, the pure in heart and the peacemakers», what kind of people are blessed? | Loud people who win every game | Rich people who own castles | People who never leave home | *People the world often overlooks
test: A friend steps between two pupils and helps them listen to each other. What is the friend doing? | Losing the argument | Ignoring both pupils | Starting a fight | *Being a peacemaker
exam: Which sentence uses peacemaker correctly? | He is a peacemaker because he loves to shout at people | The peacemaker threw the ball at the window | *Ayesha acted as peacemaker when the two boys began to argue | Peacemaker is the name of a fish
